            <ArticleTitle>Reduced lung diffusion capacity in type 2 diabetes is independent of heart failure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e73-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.diabres.2012.02.014</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In a case-control analysis comparing 303 patients with diabetes and 303 without (matched on age, race, sex and height), diabetics had reduced lung diffusion (DLCO) independent of smoking, obesity, clinical heart failure, asymptomatic left ventricular systolic and diastolic dysfunction: DLCO (mean±SE: 15.5±0.9 vs. 16.4 ±0.9, p=0.01).</AbstractText>
